{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Treasure</b> — a general term for all that a man stores of good foods, and he mentioned oil alone, for it is the most praiseworthy of all, by which Elohim and men are honored. Because of its fine richness, it is set as the first of the trees, and the proof is that the wise man stores it and does not consume it." "<b>And the fool</b> — opposite the wise man, for as soon as he acquires it he devours it. And if 'fool' is adjacent to 'man,' it is [in] construct state, like זובח אדם, or 'the man' is the fool, and both are correct."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:02.082350340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}